High-end mobile phones have several megabytes of RAM available
to applications and more for files (flash). In addition, mobile
phones may have remote media drives, capacity of disks 64 MB - 1 GB.

Low-end mobile phones have less RAM & disk space, but then those
typically allow running only midlets.

You can play nethack with Nokia 770 Internet Tablet:
https://maemo.org/maemowiki/ApplicationCatalog. It's not a mobile phone,
but specs are quite similar to high-end phones (just larger display).
(Also, PSP has unofficial port of nethack as well.)




